# Copy this file to tailscale-oauth.env next to LocalChatServer.exe
# (or inside the server/ folder on Termux). Fill in real values. Do not
# commit tailscale-oauth.env or put it inside a shared ZIP.
#
# Tailnet name: in the admin console, open DNS. "MagicDNS" is like
#   yourname.ts.net
# Personal Gmail tailnets often use the owner email instead, e.g.
#   you@gmail.com
# A hyphen - means "the tailnet this OAuth client belongs to" and is
# usually the least error-prone choice.
#
# One Tailscale login can belong to SEVERAL tailnets, and an OAuth client only
# ever covers the one it was created in. Signing in to login.tailscale.com can
# land you on your own personal tailnet rather than the shared one, and a client
# generated there looks perfectly valid while listing machines that have nothing
# to do with this chat. Before generating the client, check the tailnet switcher
# at the top of the console and pick the tailnet whose Machines list contains
# THIS server. The server checks this for you and refuses to enforce a device
# list it cannot find itself in, so nobody is locked out by the mistake.
#
# TAILSCALE_GRACE_SECONDS is how long accounts already confirmed on the tailnet
# keep working while the server cannot reach api.tailscale.com — a phone hosting
# this server loses public DNS often enough that pausing every chat within
# seconds is the worse failure. Default 86400 (one day).
#
# The OAuth client needs the "Devices: Read" (core) scope, and the server host
# needs ordinary internet access to api.tailscale.com. Local Chat also reads the
# accepted invites of the server device, which needs the separate "Device
# invites: Read" scope on the same client. Without that scope the device-share
# call answers 404, tailnet members keep working, and share-only people have to
# be mapped by hand from the app's Activity log. With it, someone who only
# received a share of this one device is recognised automatically when they
# connect, and revoking the share suspends that Local Chat account and stops its
# notifications while preserving all chat history.
#
# If sign-in says membership cannot be verified after a restart, ask the server
# why, or turn enforcement back off:
#   python run.py tailscale-check
#   python run.py tailscale-check --disable
# The admin account can always sign in, even while that check fails.

TAILSCALE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
TAILSCALE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
TAILSCALE_TAILNET=-
TAILSCALE_GRACE_SECONDS=86400
